.TH base64 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
base64 \- base64 encode/decode data and print to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY base64
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Base64 encode or decode FILE, or standard input, to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#base64\-d
\fB\-d, \-\-decode\fP
.UE
decode data
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#base64\-i
\fB\-i, \-\-ignore\-garbage\fP
.UE
when decoding, ignore non\-alphabet characters
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#base64\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-wrap=\,COLS\fP
.UE
wrap encoded lines after COLS character (default 76).
Use 0 to disable line wrapping
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/base64#base64\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/base64#base64\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.PP
The data are encoded as described for the base64 alphabet in RFC 4648.
When decoding, the input may contain newlines in addition to the bytes of
the formal base64 alphabet.  Use \fB\-\-ignore\-garbage\fR to attempt to recover
from any other non\-alphabet bytes in the encoded stream.
